1. Enable telephony service
conf t
telephony-service
max-ephones 10
max-dn 10
ip source-address 192.168.1.1 port 2000
auto assign 1 to 10
exit
What this does:
Turns on Cisco Call Manager Express
Sets router IP as call control server
Allows phones to register automatically

2. Create extensions (Directory Numbers)
ephone-dn 1
number 1001
name DJ-Phone1

ephone-dn 2
number 1002
name DJ-Phone2

3. Configure phones (ephones)
ephone 1
mac-address 000A.41B2.C3D4
button 1:1

ephone 2
mac-address 000A.41B2.C3D5
button 1:2
What this does:
Links physical IP phones to extensions
Maps button → extension number

4. DHCP for IP phones 
ip dhcp pool VOICE
network 192.168.1.0 255.255.255.0
default-router 192.168.1.1
option 150 ip 192.168.1.1
Important:
Option 150 = tells phones where the TFTP/CME server is

5. Enable IP routing interface
interface g0/0
ip address 192.168.1.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown

6. Verify phones
show ephone registered
show telephony-service
show ephone
